ned subnets and canister execution.","source_url":"https://internetcomputer.org/whitepaper.pdf"},{"date":"2022","type":"chain_fusion","description":"Threshold-chain-key systems enabled native canister-controlled Bitcoin and later Ethereum asset integration without a conventional custodian.","source_url":"https://docs.internetcomputer.org/concepts/chain-fusion/chain-key-tokens/"},{"date":"2024-04-10","type":"tvl_peak","description":"DefiLlama''s reviewed series reached $110.8M TVL.","source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/v2/historicalChainTvl/ICP"},{"date":"2026-07-29","type":"current_snapshot","description":"ICP ranked 49th with tracked TVL 89.05% below peak and its token 99.71% below ATH.","source_url":"https://chaindump.xyz/api/chains"}]},"token":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","launch_status":"launched","token_symbol":"ICP","gas_token":"cycles","launch_date":"2021-05-10","launch_date_precision":"day","launch_relation":"ICP governs the NNS, rewards node providers/voters, and burns into XDR-pegged cycles; developers load canisters with cycles so end users do not directly pay ICP gas.","token_cg_id":"internet-computer","token_current_usd":2.06,"token_ath_usd":700.65,"token_ath_date":"2021-05-10","price_drawdown_pct":99.71,"market_cap_usd":1142362889,"fdv_usd":1142363019,"circulating_supply":555228207.6303306,"total_supply":555228270.7628601,"max_supply":null,"unlock_overhang_pct":0,"source_url":"https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/internet-computer"},"capital":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","total_raised_usd":null,"rounds":[],"treasury_usd":null,"backers_tier":"tier1","notes":"Historic DFINITY financings and token allocations predate genesis, but a reconciled primary-source total and current foundation treasury were not established in this wave."},"onchain":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","tvl_peak_usd":110842591,"tvl_peak_date":"2024-04-10","tvl_current_usd":12141935,"tvl_drawdown_pct":89.05,"stablecoin_tvl_usd":3304230.03,"spot_dex_volume_24h_usd":344696,"spot_dex_volume_30d_usd":6931542,"fees_24h_usd":1216,"fees_30d_usd":21185,"revenue_24h_usd":198,"revenue_30d_usd":2302,"active_addresses_daily":null,"dev_activity_monthly":null,"tvl_concentration":null,"source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/v2/historicalChainTvl/ICP","fees_source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/fees/ICP?dataType=dailyFees","revenue_source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/fees/ICP?dataType=dailyRevenue","volume_source_url":"https://api.llama.fi/overview/dexs/ICP?dataType=dailyVolume","stablecoin_source_url":"https://stablecoins.llama.fi/stablecoinchains","methodology_note":"DefiLlama DeFi fees do not capture all cycles burned for compute, storage, bandwidth, HTTPS outcalls, or application serving."},"team":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","founders":[{"name":"Dominic Williams","role":"DFINITY founder and chief scientist","source_url":"https://internetcomputer.org/whitepaper.pdf"}],"entity":"The DFINITY Foundation is a major protocol contributor; the NNS executes network governance and controls system canisters and subnet configuration.","key_events":[{"date":"2021-05-10","type":"genesis","description":"NNS-governed mainnet and ICP token launched.","source_url":"https://internetcomputer.org/whitepaper.pdf"},{"date":"2026","type":"tokenomics_review","description":"The Mission 70 proposal targeted at least a 70% inflation reduction as cycle burn grew but minting remained elevated.","source_url":"https://internetcomputer.org/whitepapers/mission70.pdf"}],"regulatory_status":null},"narrative":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","purpose":"Run full-stack applications, web services, DAOs, and cross-chain systems directly on a sovereign decentralized compute network.","positioning":"A subnet-based Wasm blockchain with reverse gas, chain-key cryptography, onchain protocol upgrades, and canisters that serve interactive applications.","competitors":[{"name":"Ethereum","relationship":"general-purpose smart-contract and governance competitor"},{"name":"Akash","relationship":"decentralized compute competitor"},{"name":"NEAR","relationship":"chain-abstraction and application-hosting competitor"}],"narrative_arc":"ICP recovered technically from a chaotic high-valuation launch by emphasizing full-stack compute and Chain Fusion, but token inflation, governance concentration, and limited DeFi liquidity remain persistent market concerns.","media_sentiment":"mixed_negative"},"risk":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","exploits":[],"sanctions":{"flagged":false,"detail":"No chain-level designation is asserted; archived exact-name SDN review remains open."},"extraction_flags":["nns_governance_concentration","subnet_trust","node_provider_permissioning","inflation","chain_key_systemic_risk"],"audit_status":null,"risks":[{"type":"governance_concentration","detail":"NNS stake voting controls protocol upgrades, node providers, subnet membership, economics, and system canisters; liquid-democracy following can concentrate effective votes.","source_url":"https://docs.internetcomputer.org/concepts/governance/"},{"type":"system_canister_control","detail":"NNS root, governance, registry, and lifeline canisters form a privileged upgrade hierarchy for the network''s core control plane.","source_url":"https://docs.internetcomputer.org/references/system-canisters/"},{"type":"inflation","detail":"Voting and node-provider rewards mint ICP while only cycles conversion and certain fees burn it; the project itself is pursuing a large inflation reduction.","source_url":"https://docs.internetcomputer.org/concepts/network-economics/"},{"type":"chain_key_dependency","detail":"ck-assets remove a third-party custodian but depend on subnet threshold keys, minter canisters, origin-chain verification, and NNS control.","source_url":"https://docs.internetcomputer.org/concepts/chain-fusion/chain-key-tokens/"}]},"synthesis":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","situation":"ICP retained a $1.14B token market cap but only $12.1M tracked TVL and $6.9M 30-day DEX volume; ICP was 99.71% below its launch-day ATH.","postmortem":"The launch priced expectations far ahead of adoption. Subsequent engineering delivered reverse gas, full-stack canisters, onchain upgrades, and Chain Fusion, but token inflation and application distribution have not closed the gap.","why":"ICP remains relevant because it offers capabilities conventional chains outsource—web serving, compute, storage, governance automation, and threshold cross-chain signing—while its complexity and permissioned node onboarding constrain easy comparison and adoption.","success_mechanism":"NNS assembles nodes into subnets, canisters consume stable-cost cycles, chain-key thresholds sign for external assets, and ICP staking continuously governs upgrades.","strategic_choices":["Use reverse gas so developers fund compute and users can interact without tokens.","Govern protocol upgrades and topology through the onchain NNS.","Split execution across hardware-standardized subnets.","Use threshold chain-key cryptography rather than conventional custodial bridges."],"unknowns":["Current neuron-following, voting-power, DFINITY, node-provider, and subnet concentration.","Application-level cycle burn, revenue, and user retention by major canister.","Failure and recovery guarantees for each chain-key minter and signing subnet.","Whether proposed inflation reductions preserve node capacity and governance security."],"lessons_learned":["Full-stack blockchain compute creates unique capabilities and a large control plane.","Onchain governance automation can reduce fork coordination while concentrating protocol authority.","Reverse gas improves UX but obscures comparisons based on user-paid transaction fees."],"could_differ":"Permissionless commodity node admission could improve openness but undermine the deterministic hardware and subnet performance model.","outlook":{"bull":"AI, full-stack apps, and Chain Fusion drive cycle burn faster than ICP issuance.","base":"ICP remains a technically unique but economically niche compute network.","bear":"Inflation and governance concentration 