 Labs.","source_url":"https://soneium.org/en/blog/soneium-mainnet-is-live"},{"date":"2025-06-03","type":"sequencer_terms","description":"Sony Block Solutions Labs published terms governing access to the Soneium sequencer.","source_url":"https://docs.soneium.org/docs/tos/"}],"regulatory_status":null},"narrative":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","purpose":"Bring Sony and partner entertainment, creator, gaming, and fan experiences onto an accessible Ethereum L2.","positioning":"A Sony/Startale-operated OP Stack chain using corporate IP distribution and Superchain compatibility to reach mainstream users.","competitors":[{"name":"Base","relationship":"consumer and creator L2 competitor"},{"name":"Abstract","relationship":"brand-led consumer L2 competitor"},{"name":"Ronin","relationship":"gaming and digital-asset distribution competitor"}],"narrative_arc":"Soneium converted Sony distribution into hundreds of millions of transactions and millions of wallets in year one, but DeFi capital collapsed and early IP restrictions exposed tension between an open-chain message and corporate content policy.","media_sentiment":"mixed"},"risk":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","exploits":[],"sanctions":{"flagged":false,"detail":"No chain-level designation is asserted; sequencer terms impose prohibited-use controls and archived exact-name SDN review remains open."},"extraction_flags":["centralized_sequencer","content_restriction","upgrade_key_control","bridge_risk","corporate_dependency"],"audit_status":null,"risks":[{"type":"sequencer_centralization","detail":"Soneium''s mempool is private to the sequencer and Sony Block Solutions Labs publishes contractual terms for sequencer access.","source_url":"https://docs.soneium.org/docs/builders/faq"},{"type":"content_intervention","detail":"Soneium restricted official infrastructure access for identified contracts based on IP policy, demonstrating application-level censorship capacity even if contracts remained onchain.","source_url":"https://soneium.org/en/blog/philosophy-for-responsible-innovation"},{"type":"bridge_and_upgrade_control","detail":"The canonical OP Stack deployment includes proxy admins, system configuration, portal, dispute games, and bridge contracts whose signers and thresholds were not reconciled here.","source_url":"https://docs.soneium.org/docs/builders/contracts"},{"type":"corporate_dependency","detail":"Distribution and policy are closely tied to Sony and Startale strategy, brands, and infrastructure.","source_url":"https://soneium.org/en/blog/soneium-mainnet-is-live"}]},"synthesis":{"as_of":"2026-07-29","situation":"Soneium reported 455M transactions and 5.3M active wallets for 2025, yet current TVL was only $7.9M—96.12% below peak—with $12.4M of 30-day DEX volume.","postmortem":"Corporate campaigns successfully produced wallets and transactions, but they did not preserve DeFi capital. Early IP restrictions also complicated the claim that Soneium is an unrestricted open network.","why":"Soneium gained usage through Sony entertainment IP, Startale execution, campaigns, LINE integration, and OP Stack compatibility; activity remained campaign- and ecosystem-led rather than a deep liquidity moat.","success_mechanism":"Sony channels creators and fans into applications, ETH gas avoids a new network-token barrier, and OP Stack reuses Ethereum tooling and settlement.","strategic_choices":["Use OP Stack and ETH gas rather than launch a bespoke L1 or network token.","Lead with creators, entertainment IP, and fan engagement.","Operate a centralized sequencer with explicit service terms.","Restrict official-infrastructure access to selected IP-infringing contracts."],"unknowns":["Current sequencer, batcher, proposer, challenger, proxy-admin, and bridge control thresholds.","Repeat-user retention behind the 455M transaction and 5.3M-wallet claims.","How much peak TVL came from ASTR incentives and launch campaigns.","The practical boundary between onchain permissionlessness and official RPC/sequencer/content restrictions."],"lessons_learned":["Corporate IP can generate activity without creating durable DeFi liquidity.","No native token reduces onboarding friction but limits an obvious governance path.","Infrastructure-layer content policy must be analyzed separately from smart-contract persistence."],"could_differ":"A neutral sequencer and explicit onchain governance could reduce corporate-control concerns, but would weaken Sony''s ability to enforce creator-protection policy.","outlook":{"bull":"Sony franchises convert millions of wallets into repeat paid creator experiences.","base":"Soneium remains an active corporate consumer chain with shallow DeFi.","bear":"Campaign activity fades and policy controls deter permissionless builders.","most_likely":"base"},"cause_tags":["sony_distribution","creator_economy","op_stack","content_policy","tvl_collapse"],"confidence":"high"}},"meta":{"dimension_completeness_pct":100,"data_completeness_pct":84,"confidence":"high","unsourced_fields":["capital.total_raised_usd","capital.treasury_usd","team.named_chain_founders","team.regulatory_status","risk.audit_status","risk.archived_sanctions_check","risk.current_control_thresholds","onchain.active_addresses_daily","onchain.dev_activity_monthly","onchain.tvl_concentration","synthesis.repeat_user_retention"],"last_reviewed":"2026-07-29"}}]')
),
dossiers AS (
  SELECT value AS dossier FROM dossier_seed, json_each(dossier_seed.payload)
),
dimension_rows AS (
  SELECT
    json_extract(dossier, '$.chain') AS chain,
    dimensions.key AS dimension,
    dimensions.value AS data,
    (SELECT json_group_array(json(json_extract(dossier, '$.source_catalog.' || source_keys.value)))
     FROM json_each(json_extract(dossier, '$.dimension_sources.' || dimensions.key)) AS source_keys) AS sources
  FROM dossiers, json_each(json_extract(dossier, '$.dimensions')) AS dimensions
),
meta_rows AS (
  SELECT
    json_extract(dossier, '$.chain') AS chain,
    '_meta' AS dimension,
    json_extract(dossier, '$.meta') AS data,
    (SELECT json_group_array(json(value))
     FROM json_each(json_extract(dossier, '$.source_catalog'))) AS sources
  FROM dossiers
)
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO chain_facts (chain, dimension, data, sources, updated_at)
SELECT chain, dimension, data, sources, '2026-07-29' FROM dimension_rows
UNION ALL
SELECT chain, dimension, data, sources, '2026-07-29' FROM meta_rows;
